‎## The Deeper Question
‎Most ask: "How do I get access?"
‎HakunaShortcut asks: "What infrastructure determines whether I am allowed access?"
‎
‎**Infrastructure Layers to Map:**
‎- Identity infrastructure
‎- Geographic eligibility
‎- KYC
‎- Payment rails
‎- Platform policies
‎- Distribution
‎- Account ownership
‎- Data portability
‎- Exit options
‎
‎## Vault Principle
‎**"A shortcut optimizes for entry. Infrastructure optimizes for longevity."**
‎
‎**Sharper:**
‎**"If your income depends on pretending to be someone else, you haven't built access. You've borrowed it."**
‎
‎## Core Signal
‎**"People don't always choose shortcuts because they are lazy. 
‎Sometimes they choose them because an invisible wall is blocking the legitimate route."**
‎
‎The HakunaShortcut mission is to find the wall.
‎
‎## Stoic Principle
‎Cannot control: Platform policies, geographic restrictions, payment providers, algorithms
‎Can control: Observe → Understand → Adapt → Build resilience
‎"The terrain is not obligated to become easier. The map must become better."
